# Migration files must check out with LF endings, always.
#
# The migration runner records a sha256 of each migration's bytes in
# schema_migrations and refuses to apply anything when a recorded file no
# longer hashes to what was stored — the guard that stops an already-applied
# migration being edited underneath the database.
#
# On Windows, Git's autocrlf rewrites files to CRLF on checkout. That changes
# the bytes without changing a single character of SQL, so every applied
# migration reads as drifted and the runner blocks the next migration. It did
# exactly that on 2026-08-14: all 20 applied migrations reported drift, none
# had actually been edited, and the fix was to convert them back to LF.
#
# Pinning *.sql to LF makes the checkout byte-identical on every machine, so
# the checksum means what it is supposed to mean: the SQL changed, not the
# platform.
*.sql text eol=lf
